// CotSC Batch 18 - extracted original English dialogue for friendly_arm_inn.d
// Keep existing @ numbers stable when translating.
@1 = ~Hobgoblins are practically besieging the walls of this keep. You can't feel safe anywhere these days.~
@2 = ~I heard Amn might declare a war on Baldur's Gate. If that's true, maybe I should move to Neverwinter. Or better, sail all the way to Moonshae Isles.~
@3 = ~Bentley is such a bright lad. No judgment, always cheerful. No wonder this place has such a great reputation, wouldn't you say?~
@4 = ~Let me drink in peace.~
@5 = ~Travel to Tethyr is interminably long lasting. All the threats and perils on the road are taking the toll on me.~
@6 = ~Good luck on your travels.~
@7 = ~Thar staleen, my friend. May your journey be swift and secure for you.~
@8 = ~Ach, to you as well, my friend. I see you are also burdened with weight of a mission. Here, take this. Navaer, revanthas.~
@9 = ~Leave the kitchen! I told Bentley to install some doors so people stop mistaking this place for a latrine.~
@10 = ~Welcome, friend. I hope I can call you friend because I wouldn't want an intruder with ill intent in my chamber.~
@11 = ~I didn't pay for a room to share it with bunch of vagabonds. Leave immediately.~
@12 = ~I already told you to leave! Do so now, or suffer the consequences of your insulance!~
@13 = ~I warned you!~
